    "rulings": [
      "Ruling: use authenticated decrypt+encrypt rather than native rewrap \u2014 tagged2.7.1 rewrap omits AAD. Cost if wrong: bounded plaintext exists inside adapter/provider copies; never claim server-side plaintext-free rewrap.",
      "Ruling: optional default Kms selection methods keep latest implementations compatible \u2014 unsupported pinned selection refuses before decrypt. Cost if wrong: providers must implement honest local capability/destination validation.",
      "Ruling: generic u64 pinned version with OpenBao portable i32::MAX cap \u2014 TypeInt is architecture-dependent. Cost if wrong: larger versions require separately qualified provider profile rather than truncation.",
      "Ruling: one owned Migrator admission and absolute cooperative deadline \u2014 per-HTTP limits alone cannot bound retained plaintext. Cost if wrong: hosts must share one instance and providers must yield; no hard preemption or remote cancellation promise.",
      "Final: Ruling: production/replicated custody is unqualified by this single-node fixture \u2014 native proof remains local. Cost if wrong: deployment topology needs independent recovery/custody evidence.",
      "Final: Ruling: Vault/AWS/Azure remain separate unqualified profiles \u2014 OpenBao cannot qualify their authentication/algorithms. Cost if wrong: applications cannot infer cloud support.",
      "Final: Ruling: cancellation/erasure claims cover owned local lifetime only \u2014 no remote rollback or universal memory erasure. Cost if wrong: remote effects and external plaintext copies require host handling.",
      "Final: Ruling: host authorization and conditional persistence remain host-owned \u2014 migrator only returns ciphertext. Cost if wrong: a host can authorize incorrectly or overwrite a newer source.",
      "Final: Ruling: custom Kms implementations must validate selection honestly \u2014 default methods refuse pinned selection before decrypt; custom dishonest behavior is not introspectable. Cost if wrong: invalid custom capability can acquire plaintext before failing.",
      "Final: Ruling: cooperative provider execution requires active Tokio time driver \u2014 late outcomes reject, blocking CPU is not preempted. Cost if wrong: non-yielding providers can hold resources longer than deadline.",
      "Final: Ruling: SQL and complete-extras acceptance remain open \u2014 absent public ownership/preparation boundaries are not supplied by migration. Cost if wrong: native owner tests could be mistaken for full Storage support.",
      "Final: Ruling: review does not establish integrity/full success \u2014 root must execute both gates. Cost if wrong: publication without matching graph/runtime evidence would be unsupported.",
      "Ruling: preserve inactive root compiler libraries with byte-identical verified archives before retiring working copies \u2014 restore disk reserve without native data/executable loss. Cost if wrong: needed libraries regenerate and consume reserve; old bytes remain archived."
    ]
